(:kif (comment InferencePSC "A problem solving context in which all assertions in the entire KB are initially visible.  However, down each inference path, the chain of microtheories used is required to have some common descendent microtheory which is capable of inheriting all of the microtheories in the chain.  Thus, queries made in InferencePSC in effect compute locations in the space of microtheories in which the query is satisfiable.  This context is used internally by the inference engine for certain recursive calls to itself, including forward inference.  See also EverythingPSC.")
