(:kif (comment ReformulationBackwardDirection "A meta-property of a CycLReformulatorDirective, meaning\nthat there exist two arguments in the directive such that the\nhigher-numbered arg (e.g. arg2 for a binary predicate) is the 'from'\narg, the input to the reformulator, and that the lower-numbered arg\n(e.g. arg1 for a binary predicate) is the 'to' arg, the output of the\nreformulator.  Its semantics are more fully determined by context.\nSee reformulationDirectionInMode for how this\ndirection can be used.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6202
  :original-record 5205
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
