  :original-formula (comment argAndRestQuotedIsa "A ternary ArgQuotedIsaPredicate (q.v.) used to place a specified quoted isa based argument-type constraint on a given VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places whose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number. (argAndRestQuotedIsa RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument to RELN must be a quoted instance of COL. Thus a closed formula (RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is a quoted instance of COL. See also argsQuotedIsa.")
  :original-prolog "'TINYKB-ASSERTION'(':TRUE-MON',[[],[['comment','argAndRestQuotedIsa',\"A ternary ArgQuotedIsaPredicate (q.v.) used to place a specified quoted isa based argument-type constraint on a given VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places whose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number. (argAndRestQuotedIsa RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument to RELN must be a quoted instance of COL. Thus a closed formula (RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is a quoted instance of COL. See also argsQuotedIsa.\"]]],'BookkeepingMt',[],/*HL*/['comment','argAndRestQuotedIsa',\"A ternary ArgQuotedIsaPredicate (q.v.) used to place a specified quoted isa based argument-type constraint on a given VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places whose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number. (argAndRestQuotedIsa RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument to RELN must be a quoted instance of COL. Thus a closed formula (RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is a quoted instance of COL. See also argsQuotedIsa.\"]).")

