(:kif (comment oldConstantName "This bookkeeping predicate relates a CycL constant to a former \"name\" of that constant.  More accurately, (oldConstantName CONSTANT STRING) means that the underlying data structure currently associated with the CycL expression CONSTANT was formerly associated instead with the SubL string STRING.  If CONSTANT has undergone multiple \"renames\", STRING will \nnormally be its most recent former \"name\".  While oldConstantName sentences \ncan be asserted and edited by hand, they are asserted automatically when a Rename is done in the Knowledge Base.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 10374
  :original-record 7357
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
