(:kif (comment AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate "A BinaryPredicateTypeByLogicalFeature and thus a specialization of BinaryPredicate.  A binary predicate <code>PRED<\/code> is an AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate if and only if it has the following two properties.  (i) For any <code>THING1<\/code> and <code>THING2<\/code> such that both <code>(PRED THING1 THING2)<\/code> and <code>(PRED THING2 THING1)<\/code> hold, <code>THING1<\/code>  = <code>THING2<\/code>.  (ii) <code>PRED<\/code>'s two argument-places must be \"co-satisfiable\" with respect to their (single-argument) type constraints (see cosatisfiableInArgs and NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement).\n<p>\nInstances of AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate include greaterThanOrEqualTo, parts, and subEvents.  See also the specialization AsymmetricBinaryPredicate; and cf. SymmetricBinaryPredicate.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 4704
  :original-record 4693
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate "A BinaryPredicateTypeByLogicalFeature and thus a specialization of BinaryPredicate.  A binary predicate <code>PRED<\/code> is an AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate if and only if it has the following two properties.  (i) For any <code>THING1<\/code> and <code>THING2<\/code> such that both <code>(PRED THING1 THING2)<\/code> and <code>(PRED THING2 THING1)<\/code> hold, <code>THING1<\/code>  = <code>THING2<\/code>.  (ii) <code>PRED<\/code>'s two argument-places must be \"co-satisfiable\" with respect to their (single-argument) type constraints (see cosatisfiableInArgs and NoteOnArgumentCosatisfiabilityRequirement).\n<p>\nInstances of AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate include greaterThanOrEqualTo, parts, and subEvents.  See also the specialization AsymmetricBinaryPredicate; and cf. SymmetricBinaryPredicate.")))
