osatisfiabilityRequirement.\n<p>\nFor example, divorcedFrom is an instance of AntiTransitiveBinaryPredicate.\n<p>\nNote also that, while not strictly disjoint with TransitiveBinaryPredicate (q.v.), in practice few if any reified predicates should be instances of both of these collections. An important specialization of AntiTransitiveBinaryPredicate is DirectBinaryPredicate (q.v.).\"]).")

