(:kif (comment ArgTypePredicate "The collection of ArgConstraintPredicates used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on the type of argument(s) appropriate for a given argument-place (or -places) of a given relation.  A \"type\" of argument can be specified in terms of isa or genls; see the various specializations of ArgTypePredicate for more detail. Violation of such a constraint results in an expression that is semantically malformed.  For a general explanation of semantic well-formedness, see CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.")
