(:kif (comment CommutativeRelation "An instance of RelationTypeByLogicalFeature (q.v.) and a specialization of AtLeastPartiallyCommutativeRelation (q.v.).  Each instance of CommutativeRelation <code>COMRELN<\/code> is a predicate or function that is commutative in all of its argument-places.  That is, if <code>COMRELN<\/code> is a predicate (function) that holds among (has a value <code>VAL<\/code> for) a given sequence of arguments, then <code>COMRELN<\/code> also holds among (has the same value <code>VAL<\/code> for) any permutation of that  sequence.  \n<p>\nExamples of commutative relations include PlusFn, or, bordersOn, temporallyIntersects, and teammates.  Specialization include SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  \n<p>\nNote that most relations are <i>not<\/i> commutative.  Cf. the disjoint collection  PartiallyCommutativeRelation.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 4881
  :original-record 4754
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment CommutativeRelation "An instance of RelationTypeByLogicalFeature (q.v.) and a specialization of AtLeastPartiallyCommutativeRelation (q.v.).  Each instance of CommutativeRelation <code>COMRELN<\/code> is a predicate or function that is commutative in all of its argument-places.  That is, if <code>COMRELN<\/code> is a predicate (function) that holds among (has a value <code>VAL<\/code> for) a given sequence of arguments, then <code>COMRELN<\/code> also holds among (has the same value <code>VAL<\/code> for) any permutation of that  sequence.  \n<p>\nExamples of commutative relations include PlusFn, or, bordersOn, temporallyIntersects, and teammates.  Specialization include SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  \n<p>\nNote that most relations are <i>not<\/i> commutative.  Cf. the disjoint collection  PartiallyCommutativeRelation.")))
  :original-formula (comment CommutativeRelation "An instance of RelationTypeByLogicalFeature (q.v.) and a specialization of AtLeastPartiallyCommutativeRelation (q.v.).  Each instance of CommutativeRelation <code>COMRELN<\/code> is a predicate or function that is commutative in all of its argument-places.  That is, if <code>COMRELN<\/code> is a predicate (function) that holds among (has a value <code>VAL<\/code> for) a given sequence of arguments, then <code>COMRELN<\/code> also holds among (has the same value <code>VAL<\/code> for) any permutation of that  sequence.  \n<p>\nExamples of commutative relations include PlusFn, or, bordersOn, temporallyIntersects, and teammates.  Specialization include SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  \n<p>\nNote that most relations are <i>not<\/i> commutative.  Cf. the disjoint collection  PartiallyCommutativeRelation.")
