(:kif (comment CycLClosedAtomicTerm "The collection of all closed CycLAtomicTerms.  \"Closed\" here means not containing any free (i.e. unbound) variables.  Since a variable itself is the only type of _atomic_ term that contains a variable (and contains it _free_, moreover, as a single occurrence of a variable can't bind itself), CycLClosedAtomicTerm has as instances all CycLAtomicTerms except CycLVariables.  Like all CycL atomic terms, Cycl closed atomic terms are \"denotational\" (see CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that this collection, like most instances of CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see quotedCollection).")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 4990
  :original-record 4789
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment CycLClosedAtomicTerm "The collection of all closed CycLAtomicTerms.  \"Closed\" here means not containing any free (i.e. unbound) variables.  Since a variable itself is the only type of _atomic_ term that contains a variable (and contains it _free_, moreover, as a single occurrence of a variable can't bind itself), CycLClosedAtomicTerm has as instances all CycLAtomicTerms except CycLVariables.  Like all CycL atomic terms, Cycl closed atomic terms are \"denotational\" (see CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that this collection, like most instances of CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see quotedCollection).")))
  :original-formula (comment CycLClosedAtomicTerm "The collection of all closed CycLAtomicTerms.  \"Closed\" here means not containing any free (i.e. unbound) variables.  Since a variable itself is the only type of _atomic_ term that contains a variable (and contains it _free_, moreover, as a single occurrence of a variable can't bind itself), CycLClosedAtomicTerm has as instances all CycLAtomicTerms except CycLVariables.  Like all CycL atomic terms, Cycl closed atomic terms are \"denotational\" (see CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that this collection, like most instances of CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see quotedCollection).")
  :original-prolog "'TINYKB-ASSERTION'(':TRUE-DEF',[[],[['comment','CycLClosedAtomicTerm',\"The collection of all closed CycLAtomicTerms.  \\\"Closed\\\" here means not containing any free (i.e. unbound) variables.  Since a variable itself is the only type of _atomic_ term that contains a variable (and contains it _free_, moreover, as a single occurrence of a variable can't bind itself), CycLClosedAtomicTerm has as instances all CycLAtomicTerms except CycLVariables.  Like all CycL atomic terms, Cycl closed atomic terms are \\\"denotational\\\" (see CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that this collection, like most instances of CycLExpressionType, is \\\"quoted\\\" (see quotedCollection).\"]]],'UniversalVocabularyMt',[],/*HL*/['comment','CycLClosedAtomicTerm',\"The collection of all closed CycLAtomicTerms.  \\\"Closed\\\" here means not containing any free (i.e. unbound) variables.  Since a variable itself is the only type of _atomic_ term that contains a variable (and contains it _free_, moreover, as a single occurrence of a variable can't bind itself), CycLClosedAtomicTerm has as instances all CycLAtomicTerms except CycLVariables.  Like all CycL atomic terms, Cycl closed atomic terms are \\\"denotational\\\" (see CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that this collection, like most instances of CycLExpressionType, is \\\"quoted\\\" (see quotedCollection).\"]).")

(:kif (comment CycLClosedDenotationalTerm "The collection of all closed denotational terms in the CycL language.  An expression is said to be \"closed\" if it contains no free variables (see CycLClosedExpression).  A CycL term is said to be \"denotational\" if it is the right sort of term to have a denotation (or value) in the universe of discourse (see CycLDenotationalTerm).  CycL sentences, while terms of CycL, are not considered denotational terms.  Each instance of CycLClosedDenotationalTerm is either a CycLClosedAtomicTerm (i.e. a CycLConstant or SubLAtomicTerm) or a CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm (i.e. a \"NAT\" with no free variables).  Examples of closed denotational terms include `Muffet', `(JuvenileFn Dog)', `(TheSetOf ?X (objectHasColor ?X GreenColor))', and `212'.  Note that these are also examples: `(BorderBetweenFn Canada Mexico)' (despite the fact that it fails actually to denote anything) and `(JuvenileFn isa genls JuvenileFn)'\n(despite the fact that it is not semantically well-formed).")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 4992
  :original-record 4791
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
