(:kif (comment CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm "A subcollection of both CycLClosedDenotationalTerm and CycLIndexedTerm (qq.v.).  CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm is the collection of all CycL terms that both may be reified and may denote something in the universe of discourse. It thus includes all instances of CycLConstant as well as any NAT (see CycLNonAtomicTerm) whose main functor denotes an instance of ReifiableFunction.\n<p>\nFor example, the NAT '(GovernmentFn France)' is a CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm, since GovernmentFn is a ReifiableFunction.  Similarly,  '(JuvenileFn Platypus)' is a CycL reifiable denotational term; although it is not currently reified in the KB, it is reifiable and denotational (see CycLClosedDenotationalTerm).  Finally, '(BorderBetweenFn Canada Mexico)' is a CycL reifiable denotational term; although it happens not to denote anything in the universe of discourse, it is nonetheless the kind of NAT that can and usually does denote.\n<p>\nNote that CycLVariables are not considered reifiable terms.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 5168
  :original-record 4847
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
