(:kif (comment FormulaArgFn "A binary function that returns an instance of CycLTerm when given an instance of NonNegativeInteger and an instance of CycLFormula as arguments.  (FormulaArgFn N RELATION-EXPRESSION) denotes the term appearing as the Nth argument within RELATION-EXPRESSION. (Note that RELATION-EXPRESSION may be a sentence or a NAT). For example:\n<p>\n(FormulaArgFn 2 (loves Gilbert Muffet)) and\n(FormulaArgFn 1 (BirthFn Muffet))\n<p>\nboth denote Muffet. Cf. ArgPositionFn.")
