(:kif (comment InterArgFormatPredicate "The subcollection of both InterArgConstraintPredicate and ArgFormatPredicate (qq.v.) whose instances are used to specify, for a given predicate PRED, a certain Format requirement on one of PRED's arguments (the \"dependent\" one), contingent upon one (usually, but not always, a different one) of PRED's arguments (the \"independent\" one) being an instance of (isa) a certain collection.  Currently, each instance of InterArgFormatPredicate is ternary, where its first argument (or \"arg1\") is the predicate PRED upon which the constraint is being placed, its arg2 the collection serving as the isa condition on PRED's independent argument, and its arg3 the Format that PRED's dependent argument is (conditionally) constrained to have.  The (numerically-specified) identities of the arguments of PRED's that are to serve as the independent and dependent arguments are fixed for each instance of \nInterArgFormatPredicate.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 5737
  :original-record 5038
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
