(:kif (comment PlusFn "A variable-arity MathematicalFunctionOnScalars that is an extension of the arithmetical operation of addition to measurable ScalarIntervals (q.v.) generally.  Where  <code>ADDEND1<\/code>, ..., and <code>ADDENDn<\/code> are pairwise numericallyComparable (q.v.), <code>(PlusFn ADDEND1 ... ADDENDn)<\/code> is the arithmetic sum of <code>ADDEND1<\/code>, ..., and <code>ADDENDn<\/code>.  For example, (PlusFn 2 3 4) is 9, and (PlusFn (Meter 1.5) (Meter 0.7)) is (Meter 2.2).\n<p>\nNote that the term <code>(PlusFn ADDEND1 ... ADDENDn)<\/code> is undefined if there are <code>ADDENDi<\/code> and <code>ADDENDj<\/code> (1 <code><= i,j <= n)<\/code> that are not comparable.  For example, <code>(PlusFn (MinutesDuration 1) (Meter 3))<\/code> is undefined, since (MinutesDuration 1) is a Time-Quantity and (Meter 3) is a Distance, and time-quantities are not comparable with distances.\n<p>\nFor subtraction, see DifferenceFn.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6016
  :original-record 5155
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
