(:kif (comment Thing "Thing is the \"universal collection\": the collection which, by definition, contains everything there is.  Every thing in the Cyc ontology -- every Individual (of any kind), every Set-Mathematical, and every Collection -- is an instance of (see isa) Thing.  Similarly, every collection is a subcollection of (see genls) Thing.  Trivially, Thing is both an instance of and a subcollection of itself, and is not a subcollection of any other collection.  (Note that the above reference to \"every thing in the Cyc ontology\" is <i>not<\/i> meant to be limited to things actually <i>reified<\/i> in the Cyc system, but includes (e.g.) every instance -- reified or not, known or not -- of every collection recognized by Cyc.)")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6635
  :original-record 5404
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
