ch always returns a NumericInterval rather than a MeasurableQuantity.)\n<p>\nSpecializations of UnitOfMeasure grouped by what they measure include UnitOfTime, UnitOfSpeed, and UnitOfVolume.  Other specializations are OneDimensionalUnitOfMeasure, MultiDimensionalUnitOfMeasure, UnitOfMeasureWithPrefix and UnitOfMeasureNoPrefix.\"]).")

(:kif (comment UnitProductFn "A binary UnitOfMeasureDenotingFunction that takes two UnitOfMeasure (q.v.) functions and returns the unit-of-measure function whose value for any given argument is the multiplicative \"product\" of the respective values yielded by the first two units, when one unit is applied to that same argument and the other unit is applied to 1.  That is, <code>(UnitProductFn UNIT1 UNIT2)<\/code> is the function <code>PRODUCT-FN<\/code> such that, for any number or other NumericInterval <code>NUM<\/code>, <code>(PRODUCT-FN NUM)<\/code> = <code>(TimesFn (UNIT1 NUM) (UNIT2 1))<\/code>.\n<p>\nFor example, (UnitProductFn Meter Meter) is SquareMeter; and (e.g.) (SquareMeter 5) is equal to (TimesFn (Meter 5) (Meter 1)). Also, (UnitProductFn  Kilowatt HoursDuration) is KilowattHour.\n<p>\nSee also PerFn.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6703
  :original-record 5428
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment UnitProductFn "A binary UnitOfMeasureDenotingFunction that takes two UnitOfMeasure (q.v.) functions and returns the unit-of-measure function whose value for any given argument is the multiplicative \"product\" of the respective values yielded by the first two units, when one unit is applied to that same argument and the other unit is applied to 1.  That is, <code>(UnitProductFn UNIT1 UNIT2)<\/code> is the function <code>PRODUCT-FN<\/code> such that, for any number or other NumericInterval <code>NUM<\/code>, <code>(PRODUCT-FN NUM)<\/code> = <code>(TimesFn (UNIT1 NUM) (UNIT2 1))<\/code>.\n<p>\nFor example, (UnitProductFn Meter Meter) is SquareMeter; and (e.g.) (SquareMeter 5) is equal to (TimesFn (Meter 5) (Meter 1)). Also, (UnitProductFn  Kilowatt HoursDuration) is KilowattHour.\n<p>\nSee also PerFn.")))
