(:kif (comment VariableArityRelation "A specialization of Relation.  Each instance of VariableArityRelation is a relation that can take a variable number of arguments. The degree of variability for a given such relation can be constrained using the predicates arityMin and arityMax. Examples of VariableArityRelations include the predicate different and the function PlusFn.  Thus the terms '(PlusFn 1 2)' and '(PlusFn 1 2 3)' are both well-formed. Cf. FixedArityRelation.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
