(:kif (comment argAndRestGenl "A ternary ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.) used to \nplace a specified genls based argument-type constraint on a given \nVariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places \nwhose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number.\n(argAndRestGenl RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for \nsemantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument \nto RELN must be an specialization of COL.  Thus a closed formula \n(RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is an instance of COL.  See also argsGenl and argAndRestIsa.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 7191
  :original-record 5720
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment argAndRestGenl "A ternary ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.) used to \nplace a specified genls based argument-type constraint on a given \nVariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places \nwhose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number.\n(argAndRestGenl RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for \nsemantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument \nto RELN must be an specialization of COL.  Thus a closed formula \n(RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is an instance of COL.  See also argsGenl and argAndRestIsa.")))
