(:kif (comment coExtensional "A TaxonomicSlotForCollections (q.v.) that holds between collections whose extents (see extent) are exactly the same. (coExtensional COL1 COL2) means that COL1 and COL2 have all their elements in common: every instance of (see isa) one is an instance of the other.  Note that since collections (see Collection), unlike mathematical sets (see Set-Mathematical), are \"intensionally defined\", two collections can be coextensional without thereby being identical (see equals).  See also \ncoextensionalSetOrCollections.")
