(:kif (comment constrainsArg "A MetaRelation predicate for stating that a given meta-relation is used to put an argument-type or format constraint (see e.g. ArgConstraintPredicate) on a given argument-place of a relation. (constrainsArg METARELN N) means that METARELN is always used to put a constraint on a relation's Nth argument-place.  For example, (constrainsArg arg2Isa 2) holds.  A slight deviation from the above occurs when N is 0: we take (constrainsArg METARELN 0) to mean that METARELN is used to constrain _all_ of a relation's argument-places; see e.g. argsIsa and argsGenl.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 8093
  :original-record 6078
