(:kif (comment constraint "(constraint RULE) labels a given RULE assertion as a constraint.  Constraints are typically used to verify that a given logical expectation is already true, rather than to deduce (and then add) a new formula which would satisfy the expectation.  In other words, if a rule (implies P(?X) Q(?X)) is labelled as a constraint, then when P(?X) is determined to be true, we verify that Q(?X) is already true rather than add a new argument for Q(?X) using the rule and P(?X) as justification.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 8097
  :original-record 6082
