(:kif (comment disjointWith "A TaxonomicSlot predicate that relates Collections  (q.v.) that have no instances in common. <code>(disjointWith COL1 COL2)<\/code> means that <code>COL1<\/code> is disjoint with <code>COL2<\/code>: nothing is an instance of both. That is, there is no <code>THING<\/code> such that both <code>(isa THING COL1)<\/code> and <code>(isa THING COL2)<\/code> hold. For example, <code>(disjointWith Herbivore Carnivore)<\/code> holds because no animal is both a herbivore and a carnivore. Note that disjointWith is <b>not<\/b> irreflexive (see IrreflexiveBinaryPredicate): it is possible for a collection to be disjoint with itself, though only if it is empty (i.e. has no instances). Thus, for example, <code>(disjointWith Nothing Nothing)<\/code> holds.  Cf. intersectsWith.\n<p>\nAlso note that it is quite possible for two second (or higher) order collections to be disjoint even if an instance of one collection and an instance of the other collection themselves share instances.  Consider, for example, the disjoint collections SpatialThingTypeByShape and SpatialThingTypeByDimensionality.  RoundObject is an instance of the first and ThreeDimensionalThing is an instance of the second; and any solid spherical object is an instance of both of these latter collections.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 8393
  :original-record 6308
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
