(:kif (comment distributesOutOfArg "(distributesOutOfArg <reln> <pred> <n>) is a directive to the canonicalizer that relation <reln> distrbutes out of a predicate <pred> when it appears as the top-most relation in the predicate's arg <n>.  Specifically, it denotes (distributesOutOfArg <reln> <pred> <n>) denotes that the canonicalizer will translate\n<p>\n(<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> (<reln> <arg-n1> <arg-n2> ... <arg-nm>) <arg-n+1> ..)\n<p>\ninto\n<p>\n(<reln> (<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> <arg-n1> <arg-n+1> ...)\n(<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> <arg-n2> <arg-n+1> ...)\n...\n(<pred> <arg-1> ... <arg-n-1> <arg-nm> <arg-n+1> ...))")
