(:kif (comment elementOf "A very general binary predicate that relates a thing to any set or collection (see SetOrCollection) that it is a member or element of. <code>(elementOf THING SETORCOL)<\/code> means that <code>THING<\/code> is an element of <code>SETORCOL<\/code>.  \n<p>\nelementOf is a more general relation than isa.  Whereas isa is used exclusively to talk about membership in Collections,  elementOf can also be used to talk about membership in mathematical sets (see Set-Mathematical).")
