(:kif (comment equals "The binary identity relation.  <code>(equals THING1 THING2)<\/code> means that <code>THING1<\/code> and <code>THING2<\/code> are \"numerically\" (as opposed to \"qualitatively\") identical, i.e. they are one and the same thing.  A sentence of the above form is true if and only if the terms occupying the two argument-places of 'equals' denote the same thing.")
