(:kif (comment equiv "A LogicalConnective that represents bi-directional implication in CycL.  It takes two arguments, each of which must be an instance of ELSentence-Assertible. (equiv FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2) means that FORMULA-1 is true precisely when FORMULA-2 is true; in other words, FORMULA-1 is true if and only if FORMULA-2 is true.  (An EL equiv formula is translated during canonicalization into an equivalent, less compact, conjunction of implies formulas.) See also the predicate sentenceEquiv.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 8487
  :original-record 6364
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment equiv "A LogicalConnective that represents bi-directional implication in CycL.  It takes two arguments, each of which must be an instance of ELSentence-Assertible. (equiv FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2) means that FORMULA-1 is true precisely when FORMULA-2 is true; in other words, FORMULA-1 is true if and only if FORMULA-2 is true.  (An EL equiv formula is translated during canonicalization into an equivalent, less compact, conjunction of implies formulas.) See also the predicate sentenceEquiv.")))
