(:kif (comment greaterThan "A NumericComparisonPredicate that is a generalization of the  mathematical greater-than ( > ) relation to ScalarIntervals (q.v.) of all sorts, including quantitative intervals (see NumericInterval and MeasurableQuantity) as well as point values (see ScalarPointValue).  <code>(greaterThan VALUE1 VALUE2)<\/code> means that  <code>VALUE1<\/code> is greater than <code>VALUE2<\/code> with respect to some scale that they  are both on.  More precisely, there is some TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType SCALE that both <code>VALUE1<\/code> and <code>VALUE2<\/code> are instances of and either (i) <code>SCALE<\/code> is a specialization of  NumericInterval (e.g. RealNumber) and the minimum (see minQuantValue) of <code>VALUE1<\/code> is greater than the maximum (see maxQuantValue) of <code>VALUE2<\/code> or (ii) <code>(followingValueOnScale VALUE2 VALUE1 SCALE)<\/code> holds.")
