(:kif (comment hlPrototypicalInstance "(hlPrototypicalInstance TERM COL) means that TERM is a prototypical instance of COL at the HL.  It is assumed that TERM has only two asserted assertions on it: one hlPrototypicalInstance assertion and one assertion of the form (isa TERM COL).  The CycInferenceEngine makes use of the prototypical instance during assertions to cache the work done by forward inference.  It is used when asserting the first isa assertion on a term with no other assertions about it yet.  <b>Do not assert comments, cyclistNotes or any other assertions on prototypical instances.<\/b>  They are intentionally minimal.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 9056
  :original-record 6621
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
