(:kif (comment interArgResultGenl "A quaternary MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly genls based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (interArgResultGenls FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC, then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the InterArgTypePredicates, interArgResultGenl _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but less flexible ternary interArg1ResultGenls et al.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 9698
  :original-record 6977
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment interArgResultGenl "A quaternary MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly genls based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (interArgResultGenls FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC, then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the InterArgTypePredicates, interArgResultGenl _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but less flexible ternary interArg1ResultGenls et al.")))
  :original-formula (comment interArgResultGenl "A quaternary MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly genls based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (interArgResultGenls FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC, then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the InterArgTypePredicates, interArgResultGenl _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but less flexible ternary interArg1ResultGenls et al.")
  :original-prolog "'TINYKB-ASSERTION'(':TRUE-DEF',[[],[['comment','interArgResultGenl',\"A quaternary MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly genls based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (interArgResultGenls FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC, then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the InterArgTypePredicates, interArgResultGenl _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but less flexible ternary interArg1ResultGenls et al.\"]]],'UniversalVocabularyMt',[],/*HL*/['comment','interArgResultGenl',\"A quaternary MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly genls based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (interArgResultGenls FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC, then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the InterArgTypePredicates, interArgResultGenl _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but less flexible ternary interArg1ResultGenls et al.\"]).")

