(:kif (comment ist "This predicate relates a microtheory to any sentence that is true in it.  (ist MT SENT) means that the CycL sentence SENT (or, if you prefer, the proposition SENT expresses) is true in the microtheory MT.  Note that SENT need not actually be _asserted_ in MT; MT might for example \"inherit\" SENT from a more general microtheory.  (Cf. ist-Asserted.)")
