(:kif (comment pointQuantValue "A NumericComparisonPredicate and a specialization of numericallyEquals, minQuantValue, and maxQuantValue (qq.v.).  pointQuantValue is essentially the relation numericallyEquals restricted to scalar point-values, with the additional proviso that its first argument must be given using a reifiable CycL term.  Thus a sentence of the form\n<p>\n\t<code>(pointQuantValue REIFIABLE-TERM OTHER-TERM)<\/code>\n<p>\nis true if and only if <code>REIFIABLE-TERM<\/code> is a CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm (q.v.), and <code>REIFIABLE-TERM<\/code> and <code>OTHER-TERM<\/code> denote the same ScalarPointValue (q.v.).\n<p>\nThis predicate is primarily used to state the equivalence of a reified scalar-denoting term (e.g. 'Zero', 'AvogadrosNumber', 'SpeedOfLight') with an appropriate unreifiable term.  For example, both of the following sentences hold:\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (pointQuantValue Zero 0)\n<\/pre>\n<p>\n<pre>\n  (pointQuantValue\n    SpeedOfLight\n    (PerFn (Mile 186000) (HoursDuration 1))'  .\n<\/pre>")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
