(:kif (comment relationExistsInstance "A ternary RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate holds between some instance of a given collection and a given thing.  <code>(relationExistsInstance BINPRED COL THING)<\/code> means that there exists an instance <code>INST<\/code> of <code>COL<\/code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST THING)<\/code> holds.  This is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n(thereExists ?INST\n  (and\n     (isa ?INST COL)\n     (PRED ?INST THING))) .\n<\/pre>\n<p>\nFor example, (relationExistsInstance eventOccursAt IllegalDrugActivity Sweden) means that there exists illegal drug activity in Sweden.  See also the shared  NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 11046
  :original-record 7617
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment relationExistsInstance "A ternary RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate holds between some instance of a given collection and a given thing.  <code>(relationExistsInstance BINPRED COL THING)<\/code> means that there exists an instance <code>INST<\/code> of <code>COL<\/code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST THING)<\/code> holds.  This is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n(thereExists ?INST\n  (and\n     (isa ?INST COL)\n     (PRED ?INST THING))) .\n<\/pre>\n<p>\nFor example, (relationExistsInstance eventOccursAt IllegalDrugActivity Sweden) means that there exists illegal drug activity in Sweden.  See also the shared  NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")))
  :original-formula (comment relationExistsInstance "A ternary RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate holds between some instance of a given collection and a given thing.  <code>(relationExistsInstance BINPRED COL THING)<\/code> means that there exists an instance <code>INST<\/code> of <code>COL<\/code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST THING)<\/code> holds.  This is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n(thereExists ?INST\n  (and\n     (isa ?INST COL)\n     (PRED ?INST THING))) .\n<\/pre>\n<p>\nFor example, (relationExistsInstance eventOccursAt IllegalDrugActivity Sweden) means that there exists illegal drug activity in Sweden.  See also the shared  NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
  :original-prolog "'TINYKB-ASSERTION'(':TRUE-DEF',[[],[['comment','relationExistsInstance',\"A ternary RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate holds between some instance of a given collection and a given thing.  <code>(relationExistsInstance BINPRED COL THING)<\/code> means that there exists an instance <code>INST<\/code> of <code>COL<\/code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST THING)<\/code> holds.  This is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n(thereExists ?INST\n  (and\n     (isa ?INST COL)\n     (PRED ?INST THING))) .\n<\/pre>\n<p>\nFor example, (relationExistsInstance eventOccursAt IllegalDrugActivity Sweden) means that there exists illegal drug activity in Sweden.  See also the shared  NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.\"]]],'UniversalVocabularyMt',[],/*HL*/['comment','relationExistsInstance',\"A ternary RuleMacroPredicate (q.v.) that can be used to state that a given binary predicate holds between some instance of a given collection and a given thing.  <code>(relationExistsInstance BINPRED COL THING)<\/code> means that there exists an instance <code>INST<\/code> of <code>COL<\/code> such that <code>(BINPRED INST THING)<\/code> holds.  This is equivalent to (and can thus be used in effect as shorthand for) the more complex form:\n<p>\n<pre>\n(thereExists ?INST\n  (and\n     (isa ?INST COL)\n     (PRED ?INST THING))) .\n<\/pre>\n<p>\nFor example, (relationExistsInstance eventOccursAt IllegalDrugActivity Sweden) means that there exists illegal drug activity in Sweden.  See also the shared  NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.\"]).")

