(:kif (comment resultGenl "A MetaFunction that is used to specify that a \ngiven collection is a supercollection of any value returned by a given CollectionDenotingFunction (q.v.).  <code>(resultGenl COLFUNC COL)<\/code> means that when <code>COLFUNC<\/code> is applied to any sequence of arguments <code>ARGS<\/code> for which it is defined, the resulting value will be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is, <code>(genls (COLFUNC . ARGS) COL)<\/code> holds.  \n<p>\nFor example, <code>(resultGenl UsingAFn Action)<\/code> implies that the collection of acts done using any given type of object is a type of action, <code>(resultGenl AttemptingFn PurposefulAction)<\/code> implies that the attempts at a given type of action constitute a type of purposeful act, and <code>(resultGenl JointTypeBetweenFn Joint-Physical)<\/code> means that the collection of joints between two given types of things is a type of physical joint.  \n<p>\nSee also resultIsa.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 11225
  :original-record 7708
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment resultGenl "A MetaFunction that is used to specify that a \ngiven collection is a supercollection of any value returned by a given CollectionDenotingFunction (q.v.).  <code>(resultGenl COLFUNC COL)<\/code> means that when <code>COLFUNC<\/code> is applied to any sequence of arguments <code>ARGS<\/code> for which it is defined, the resulting value will be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is, <code>(genls (COLFUNC . ARGS) COL)<\/code> holds.  \n<p>\nFor example, <code>(resultGenl UsingAFn Action)<\/code> implies that the collection of acts done using any given type of object is a type of action, <code>(resultGenl AttemptingFn PurposefulAction)<\/code> implies that the attempts at a given type of action constitute a type of purposeful act, and <code>(resultGenl JointTypeBetweenFn Joint-Physical)<\/code> means that the collection of joints between two given types of things is a type of physical joint.  \n<p>\nSee also resultIsa.")))
  :original-formula (comment resultGenl "A MetaFunction that is used to specify that a \ngiven collection is a supercollection of any value returned by a given CollectionDenotingFunction (q.v.).  <code>(resultGenl COLFUNC COL)<\/code> means that when <code>COLFUNC<\/code> is applied to any sequence of arguments <code>ARGS<\/code> for which it is defined, the resulting value will be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is, <code>(genls (COLFUNC . ARGS) COL)<\/code> holds.  \n<p>\nFor example, <code>(resultGenl UsingAFn Action)<\/code> implies that the collection of acts done using any given type of object is a type of action, <code>(resultGenl AttemptingFn PurposefulAction)<\/code> implies that the attempts at a given type of action constitute a type of purposeful act, and <code>(resultGenl JointTypeBetweenFn Joint-Physical)<\/code> means that the collection of joints between two given types of things is a type of physical joint.  \n<p>\nSee also resultIsa.")
  :original-prolog "'TINYKB-ASSERTION'(':TRUE-DEF',[[],[['comment','resultGenl',\"A MetaFunction that is used to specify that a \ngiven collection is a supercollection of any value returned by a given CollectionDenotingFunction (q.v.).  <code>(resultGenl COLFUNC COL)<\/code> means that when <code>COLFUNC<\/code> is applied to any sequence of arguments <code>ARGS<\/code> for which it is defined, the resulting value will be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is, <code>(genls (COLFUNC . ARGS) COL)<\/code> holds.  \n<p>\nFor example, <code>(resultGenl UsingAFn Action)<\/code> implies that the collection of acts done using any given type of object is a type of action, <code>(resultGenl AttemptingFn PurposefulAction)<\/code> implies that the attempts at a given type of action constitute a type of purposeful act, and <code>(resultGenl JointTypeBetweenFn Joint-Physical)<\/code> means that the collection of joints between two given types of things is a type of physical joint.  \n<p>\nSee also resultIsa.\"]]],'UniversalVocabularyMt',[],/*HL*/['comment','resultGenl',\"A MetaFunction that is used to specify that a \ngiven collection is a supercollection of any value returned by a given CollectionDenotingFunction (q.v.).  <code>(resultGenl COLFUNC COL)<\/code> means that when <code>COLFUNC<\/code> is applied to any sequence of arguments <code>ARGS<\/code> for which it is defined, the resulting value will be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is, <code>(genls (COLFUNC . ARGS) COL)<\/code> holds.  \n<p>\nFor example, <code>(resultGenl UsingAFn Action)<\/code> implies that the collection of acts done using any given type of object is a type of action, <code>(resultGenl AttemptingFn PurposefulAction)<\/code> implies that the attempts at a given type of action constitute a type of purposeful act, and <code>(resultGenl JointTypeBetweenFn Joint-Physical)<\/code> means that the collection of joints between two given types of things is a type of physical joint.  \n<p>\nSee also resultIsa.\"]).")

