(:kif (comment resultIsaArg "A MetaRelation predicate.  <code>(resultIsaArg FUNC N)<\/code>  means that the value returned by <code>FUNC<\/code> for any given sequence of arguments  is an instance of the <code>N<\/code>th argument in that sequence.  That is, if  <code>(FUNC ARG1 ... ARGN ...) = VALUE<\/code>, then <code>(isa VALUE ARGN)<\/code> holds.  Obviously, <code>ARGN<\/code> must be a collection; so <code>FUNC<\/code>'s <code>N<\/code>th argument-place is likely to be constrained (via argIsa) to be an instance of Collection or some specialization thereof.\n<p>\nFor example, (resultIsaArg The 1) entails that (The Dog) is an instance of Dog.\n<p>\nSee also resultGenlArg and resultIsa.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 11266
  :original-record 7731
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
  :original-cnf (() ((comment resultIsaArg "A MetaRelation predicate.  <code>(resultIsaArg FUNC N)<\/code>  means that the value returned by <code>FUNC<\/code> for any given sequence of arguments  is an instance of the <code>N<\/code>th argument in that sequence.  That is, if  <code>(FUNC ARG1 ... ARGN ...) = VALUE<\/code>, then <code>(isa VALUE ARGN)<\/code> holds.  Obviously, <code>ARGN<\/code> must be a collection; so <code>FUNC<\/code>'s <code>N<\/code>th argument-place is likely to be constrained (via argIsa) to be an instance of Collection or some specialization thereof.\n<p>\nFor example, (resultIsaArg The 1) entails that (The Dog) is an instance of Dog.\n<p>\nSee also resultGenlArg and resultIsa.")))
