(:kif (comment sentenceEquiv "(sentenceEquiv FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2) means that  the ELSentence-Assertible FORMULA-1 is logically equivalent to the ELSentence-Assertible FORMULA-2.  This predicate is very similar to equiv, but equiv is an instance of LogicalConnective, while sentenceEquiv is an instance of Predicate.  sentenceEquiv is primarily intended to be used for rules that quantify over CycL formulas.")
  :monotonicity :DEFAULT
  :original-tv :TRUE-DEF
