(:kif (comment ArgQuotedIsaBinaryPredicate "A specialization of ArgQuotedIsaPredicate . Each instance of ArgQuotedIsaBinaryPredicate takes a Relation RELN as its first argument, and a SubLExpressionType Collection COL as its second argument, and places a constraint based on COL on at least one of the argument-places of RELN. To be more precise, suppose that PRED is an ArgIsaBinaryPredicate that specifies an argument-type for the Nth argument-place of RELN. Then a sentence of the form (PRED RELN COL) entails that a closed formula of the form (RELN ... ARGN ...) is semantically well-formed only if ARGN is an instance (i.e. quotedIsa) of COL.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 4735
  :original-record 4710
