(:kif (comment RelationExistsAllFn "The predicate relationExistsAll states that for every instance of a collection, some other term exists in a certain relationship.  An arbitrary such term is a function of the instance, the predicate, the collection, and the type of the other term.  (RelationExistsAllFn TERM PRED DEP-COL INDEP-COL) allows one to denote this `arbitrary such term that so exists' in a named fashion.")
