(:kif (comment SubLQuoteFn "<code>(SubLQuoteFn SUBL-EXPRESSION)<\/code> is one of exactly two escapes to SubL from CycL, the other being ExpandSubLFn.  These are the only two ways to represent arbitrary SubL in CycL.  SubLQuoteFn encapsulates <code>SUBL-EXPRESSION<\/code> such that it will not be rejected by the CycL wff-checker as ill-formed CycL.  For example, <code>(SubLQuoteFn (+ 1 2))<\/code>, which <i>is<\/i> a CycLExpression, denotes the SubLSExpression (+ 1 2), which itself is <i>not<\/i> a CycLExpression.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6540
  :original-record 5337
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
