(:kif (comment WFFConstraintPredicate "The collection of all Predicates which can impose well-formedness constraints.  More specifically, only assertions of the form (PRED . ARGS), where PRED is an instance of WFFConstraintPredicate, can directly impose a well-formedness constraint, i.e. cause a previously well-formed sentence to become ill-formed, given the same WFF standards.  Any assertion could _indirectly_ impose a well-formedness constraint, for instance by triggering a forward rule or an afterAdding.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
