(:kif (comment WFFConstraintSatisfactionPredicate "The collection of all Predicates which can satisfy well-formedness constraints.  More specifically, only assertions of the form (PRED . ARGS), where PRED is an instance of WFFConstraintPredicate, can directly satisfy a well-formedness constraint, i.e. cause any previously ill-formed sentence to become well-formed, given the same WFF standards.  Any assertion could _indirectly_ satisfy a well-formedness constraint, for instance by triggering a forward rule or an afterAdding.  A common case of this is the afterAddings on spec-preds of isa and genls.")
