(:kif (comment admittedAllArgument "A ternary MetaRelation predicate that relates a Collection to an integer (representing an argument-place) to a Relation such that every instance of the collection is an admittedArgument (q.v.) to the specified argument-place of the relation.  <code>(admittedAllArgument COL ARGNUM RELN)<\/code> means that every instance of <code>COL<\/code> satisfies all of the (single-argument) argument-type constraints (see ArgIsaPredicate and ArgGenlPredicate) for the <code>ARGNUM<\/code>th argument position of <code>RELN<\/code>.  Note that <code>COL<\/code> is required <i>not<\/i> to be an  EmptyCollection.\n<p>\nFor example, <code>(admittedAllArgument FemaleHuman 1 spouse)<\/code> and <code>(admittedAllArgument PersonTypeByActivity 1 JuvenileFn)<\/code> both hold.")
