(:kif (comment admittedSentence "(admittedSentence SENTENCE) states that SENTENCE is a CycLSentence which is both syntactically and semantically well-formed with respect to argument constraints only.  For example, (admittedSentence (bordersOn Canada France)) is true in WorldGeographyDualistMt, but not in WorldGeographyMt, since Canada and France are known to be instances of GeographicalRegion in the former microtheory, but not in the latter microtheory.  See also admittedArgument.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6865
  :original-record 5490
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
