(:kif (comment arg1Genl "A binary ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(arg1Genl RELN COL)<\/code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the first argument to <code>RELN<\/code> must be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is, <code>(RELN ARG1<\/code> ...) is semantically well-formed only if <code>(genls ARG1 COL)<\/code> holds.  For an  explanation of semantic well-formedness, see CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See argGenl for a similar but more flexible  ternary predicate.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 6894
  :original-record 5517
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
