(:kif (comment arg1SometimesIsa "An ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(arg1SometimesIsa RELATION\nCOLLECTION)<\/code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything\ngiven as the first argument to <code>RELATION<\/code> must be an instance of\n<code>COLLECTION<\/code> at some time.  More precisely, if\n<code>(arg1SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)<\/code> holds then in order to\nassert <code>(RELATION ARG1 ...)<\/code>, it must only be the case that there\nexists some time interval (including Always-TimeInterval) in which\n<code>(isa ARG1 COLLECTION)<\/code> holds.")
