(:kif (comment arg3SometimesIsa "An ArgSometimesIsaPredicate and ArgTypeBinaryPredicate, <code>(arg3SometimesIsa\nRELATION COLLECTION)<\/code> means that semantic well-formedness requires that\nanything given as the third argument to <code>RELATION<\/code> must be an\ninstance of <code>COLLECTION<\/code> at some time.  More precisely, if\n<code>(arg3SometimesIsa RELATION COLLECTION)<\/code> holds then in order to\nassert <code>(RELATION ... ARG3 ...)<\/code>, it must only be the case that there\nexists some time interval (including Always-TimeInterval) in which\n<code>(isa ARG3 COLLECTION)<\/code> holds.")
