(:kif (comment arg4Genl "A binary ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.).  <code>(arg4Genl RELN COL)<\/code>  means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the fourth argument to <code>RELN<\/code> must be a subcollection of <code>COL<\/code>.  That is,  <code>(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ...)<\/code> is semantically well-formed only if  <code>(genls ARG4 COL)<\/code> holds.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see  CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.  See argGenl for a  similar but more flexible ternary predicate.")
