(:kif (comment argQuotedIsa "A ternary Predicate (argQuotedIsa RELN N COL) means that semantic well-formedness requires that the term given as the Nth argument to RELN must be an instance of the SubLExpressionType COL. That is, (RELN ... ARGN ...) is semantically well-formed only if (quotedIsa ARGN COL) holds. For example, (argQuotedIsa examplePredSentences 1 CycLSentence) holds. ")
