(:kif (comment backchainRequired "(backchainRequired PREDICATE) means that rules that conclude PREDICATE must be used in order to prove literals involving PREDICATE.  In other words, when performing inferences, all literals involving PREDICATE must be eliminated using rules since there won't be any other way to prove them.  See also backchainEncouraged, backchainDiscouraged, and backchainForbidden.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 7498
  :original-record 5883
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
