(:kif (comment evaluationResultQuotedIsa "A binary MetaRelation that holds between relations and collections. evaluationResultQuotedIsa is primarily used to indicate that any value returned by a given evaluatable function is a quoted instance of a given collection. Where FUNC is a Function-Denotational, (evaluationResultQuotedIsa FUNC COL) means that FUNC returns a quoted instance of COL for any sequence of arguments for which FUNC is defined. That is, (quotedIsa (FUNC ARG1 ... ARGn) COL) holds for any sequence <ARG1, ..., ARGN> for which FUNC has a value. For example, '(evaluationResultQuotedIsa SubstringFn SubLString)' holds, and it entails (e.g.) '(quotedIsa (SubstringFn \"ABC\" 1 2) SubLString)'.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 8519
  :original-record 6388
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
  :original-variable-names ()
  :converted-variable-names ()
  :converted-row-variable-names ()
