(:kif (comment ist-Asserted "A MicrotheoryDesignatingPredicate that is used to relate CycL sentences to microtheories in which they are explicitly asserted. (ist-Asserted MT SENT) states that there is a CycLAssertion for SENT in the Microtheory MT.  This predicate is therefore a more specialized form of ist (q.v.) with the additional requirement that there be an actual assertion for SENT in MT.\n<p>\nNote that the above is also more precise than (ist MT (assertedSentence SENT)), which states that there is an assertion for SENT in some microtheory visible from (see genlMt) MT.")
  :monotonicity :MONOTONIC
  :original-tv :TRUE-MON
  :original-source-file "tiny_kb.pldata"
  :original-source-line 9784
  :original-record 7051
  :original-form-levels (:HL)
