(:kif (comment reformulatorRule "(reformulatorRule EXPR-1 EXPR-2), asserted in the\nmicrotheory MT, means that EXPR-1 may be reformulated into EXPR-2 (or\nvice versa, based on meta-properties of this rule and what mode the\nreformulator is in) in MT\nor a specMt thereof.  Free variables in EXPR-1 and EXPR-2 are shared,\nand may bind with CycL expressions which match the template. Truth\nand semantics are not necessarily preserved (see TruthPreservingReformulation).\nUse the more specific predicates reformulatorEquiv and reformulatorEquals\nwhen applicable.")
